Subject: GHSA-2mjx-qc3c-rqvc: pin rustls 0.23.45 in Cargo.lock

Vaultwarden 1.37.3 locks rustls 0.23.44. Rustls 0.23.13 through 0.23.44
accepts TLS 1.3 handshake messages that cross an encryption-level change
inside one record. 0.23.45 rejects them. The crate's dependency set is
unchanged from 0.23.44 (webpki ^0.103.14, already locked at 0.103.15), so
this patch only moves the rustls version, its crates.io checksum, and the
six lockfile edges that name rustls 0.23.44.

Advisory: https://github.com/rustls/rustls/security/advisories/GHSA-2mjx-qc3c-rqvc
Tracker: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0285.html
Upstream source: https://github.com/rustls/rustls/releases/tag/v/0.23.45
Checksum: crates.io sparse index cksum for rustls 0.23.45
(0d41d731c7d2f962d1ccc364cec258de3c0e93b38c2fb3ba97ac74513048d634).
Reproduce from the 1.37.3 Cargo.lock with cargo update -p rustls@0.23.44
--precise 0.23.45. rustls 0.21.12, required by rocket_http 0.5.1, is left
as-is.

